  "notes": [
    "patch_softmute.s, patch_mutemode.s, manifest.py and runtime.json are byte for byte modwerk-modules/mute-modes/ at 72d115f01299ce518dc4ada580b1adde96813e89, the head of the owner's (repeat98) pull request Zac-Kyoti/octatrack-kyoti-fw#5, branch mute-modes-0.2.4-rest of repeat98/octatrack-kyoti-fw. That pull request is not merged: the owner waived the author's upstream merge for this version on 26 November 2026, so the commit is imported from the pull request's head, not from the author's main. Its parent is the author's 211055b5649cc897f7dec831125eec9404a64e40. patch_mutemode.s and manifest.py are unchanged from 00897f0. upstream/README.md, LICENSE and upstream/OCTABAM_LICENSE are unchanged from 0.1.0's record.",
    "0.2.4 rests while MUTE MODE is OT, the default. mm_in_use answers the base's ev_in_use (order 50) from the UI tick: 0 while GATE is 0, after doing pre's OT clear of UNHELD and SHADOW itself, so a track still muted when MUTE MODE leaves OT is held as before when the module wakes; 1 for OTFX, OTFX-T, DT-T or an unknown value. runtime.json lists five detours as rests (0x40004dc6, 0x40006844, 0x4000f4dc, 0x4000d498, 0x40004c72); fresh_bind (0x40006820) is not one, as ev_voice_bind replaces it, and the table pointer and count sites never rest. The code sits under MODWERK_EVENTS only: the native units (plain 996 B, SC_KEY 1106 B) and every author reference are unchanged.",
    "The stock guard digests are 0.1.0's; no hook site changed."
  ],
